course: dictionary
lesson: 3097
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Egg is one of them. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is meant. «A dozen eggs» means twelve eggs, and here egg is a thing you buy and count.
explain: «A butterfly's life cycle is egg, caterpillar, chrysalis and adult butterfly.» Here egg is the first stage of life. It is what an insect lays, and the baby grows inside it. The clue is the word life cycle, which tells you the sentence is about how a creature grows.
explain: Look at the words around the word. Does the sentence talk about food, nests, babies or sweets? Swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense. A chocolate egg at Easter is a treat, not a thing a bird lays.
fact: An egg is the round or oval thing a hen lays, and people eat it.
fact: Birds, fish, frogs, insects and reptiles also lay eggs, and their babies grow inside them.
fact: A chocolate egg is a sweet, often eaten at Easter.
fact: «A dozen eggs» means twelve eggs, because a dozen is always 12.
fact: Context means the words around a word; they often tell you which meaning to use.
exercise: What is «a dozen eggs»? | Six eggs | One big egg | Ten eggs | *Twelve eggs
exercise: «A butterfly's life cycle is egg, caterpillar, chrysalis and adult butterfly.» Here egg means | A kind of nest box | *The first stage of life, laid by an insect | A chocolate treat at Easter | A round thing a hen lays and people eat
exercise: Which animal lays eggs? | *A frog | A horse | A dog | A cow
test: Tom had a boiled egg for breakfast. Which meaning of egg is this? | A box for birds to nest in | A chocolate egg at Easter | *A round thing a hen lays, which people eat | The first stage of an insect's life
test: Birds, fish, frogs, insects and reptiles all lay eggs. What happens inside them? | *Their babies grow inside | They are eaten at Easter | They are sold by the dozen | They are painted with patterns
exam: In «Pysanky are Ukrainian Easter eggs decorated with wax and dye», what kind of egg is meant? | *An egg, decorated for Easter | A dozen eggs | A nest box for birds | A chocolate egg
